# ARR bridge, FY26

A subtotal is arithmetic, not an observation: a row flagged by `total` is drawn
from the baseline to the running total as the steps above it left it, and its
own value cell is not read. So only the closing balance is flagged. The opening
balance is the walk's first step — a rise from zero — because a bridge that
began at a subtotal would begin at nothing. Connectors carry the running balance
between bars so the walk is legible as one continuous quantity, and direction
uses the status palette because increase and decrease are a fixed vocabulary of
two, never palette slots.

```mdv waterfall
title: ARR bridge (thousands)
category: step
value: delta
total: subtotal
connector: true
format: table
---
step          | delta | subtotal
Opening ARR   | 18400 | false
New business  |  5240 | false
Expansion     |  2180 | false
Contraction   |  -940 | false
Churn         | -1610 | false
Closing ARR   | 23270 | true
```
